<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Glenn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921–2016</span> · Also known as John H. Glenn Jr.</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Glenn was an American astronaut and politician. On 20 February 1962, in the capsule Friendship 7, he became the first American to orbit the Earth, circling it three times; after splashing down in the Atlantic he was debriefed on Grand Turk. He later served as a senator from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a> from 1974 to 1999, and in 1998, aged 77, he flew on the Space Shuttle Discovery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-glenn.jpg" alt="John Glenn" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Senate Historical Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Glenn_Low_Res.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
